#: ../../tools/drug_properties_tools.rst:32 0133699b3468426290e29d479ca3aa61
msgid ""
"**Description**: Calculate Quantitative Estimate of Drug-likeness (QED) "
"score for a compound using the Bickerton et al. (2012) method. QED "
"integrates 8 molecular descriptors (MW, AlogP, HBA, HBD, PSA, rotatable "
"bonds, aromatic rings, structural alerts) into a single score from 0 "
"(non-drug-like) to 1 (most drug-like). Median QED of approved oral drugs "
"is ~0.49. High QED (≥0.67) = drug-like; Medium (0.34–0.67) = borderline; "
"Low (<0.34) = non-drug-like. Use after DrugProps\\_lipinski\\_filter for "
"a more nuanced drug-likeness assessment."
msgstr ""

